Why a licence of its own: the mu-plugin and the object-cache drop-in run
inside WordPress, on its hooks and in place of its object cache, and the
WordPress Foundation regards such code as a derivative of WordPress, which is
GPL-2.0-or-later. They are installed into every WordPress site CloudGround
hosts, so they carry WordPress's licence whatever licence the rest of
CloudGround has. The Go code in this directory (connector.go,
connector_test.go) only embeds these files and is under the repository's
licence.
